# DSAP-SMF (Simple Management Framework)

Retro Linksys / early-2000s web admin design system for Dreamscape DSAP applets (`*.dyna.dreamscape.jp`, `ispy.dreamscape.jp`, `dreamscape.jp` home).

## Assets

| Asset | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `public/css/dsap-smf.css` | Tokenized shared styles scoped under `.dsap-smf` + `[data-dsap]` with legacy class aliases |
| `public/scripts/comp/dsapSmfMarkup.js` | Global markup builders (no modules) |
| `theme: 'dsap-smf'` on `registerDsap` | Lazy-injects shared CSS via `dsapRegistry.js` |

Loaded at startup in `app.html` (after `dsapRegistry.js`):

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/dsap-smf.css">
<script src="scripts/comp/dsapSmfMarkup.js"></script>
```

## Page layout (top → bottom)

```
| Branch (left)     | Tool (right)      |  ← 2-column header
|---------------------------------------------------|
| Tabs / sections                                   |  ← tab bar (table-based canonical)
|---------------------------------------------------|
| Toolbar / context for active tab                  |
|---------------------------------------------------|
| Page content                                      |
```

### Header bar — **two columns ONLY**

Reference: `dsapSmfBuildHeader()` + `public/css/dsap-smf.css`.

**Exactly 2 `<td>` cells** per header row: branch/system name (left) | active tab name (right). No third column.

| Column | Class | Width | Purpose |
|--------|-------|-------|---------|
| Left | `.dsap-smf-header-branch` | 65% | Static branch / system name for the applet (e.g. Security Center, Data Management, Enshutsuka) |
| Right | `.dsap-smf-header-tool` | 35% | **Dynamic active tab label** — updates when the user switches tabs |

```javascript
dsapSmfBuildHeader({
  branchTitle: DSAP_SMF_BRANCH_DATA_MGMT,
  toolTitle: 'Status',
  toolTitleId: 'dsapSmfHeaderTool'  // optional; default id for dsapSmfUpdateHeaderTool
});

// On tab switch (init/refresh or view sync):
dsapSmfUpdateHeaderTool(root, 'Workspaces');
```

**Forbidden in headers**

- Third `<td>` / middle context column
- `contextSubtitle`, `headerContextId`, `.dsap-smf-header-context`
- Putting the applet name on the right while the tab name sits on the left (e.g. `Dreamscape Administration | Security Center`)
- 3-column width rules (e.g. 45% / 30% / 25%)

Tab names belong in the **right header cell** and in the tab bar — not duplicated as a third header column. Workspace/scope hints use the optional context bar below tabs.

Branch constants live in `dsapSmfMarkup.js` (`DSAP_SMF_BRANCH_*`).

