## Pickers: context menu (not custom-dropdown)

SMF applets use **`contextMenu.attachClickMenuToElement`** for filter/picker buttons (per-page, workspace, enum settings). Follow the filter picker pattern in `omegasearchDsapApplet.js`.

- Trigger: `dsap-smf-btn` + caret icon
- Wire in `setTimeout(..., 0)` after HTML is in the DOM
- Teardown: `contextMenu.detachClickMenuFromElement` in `destroy()`
- Do **not** use `custom-dropdown` / `setupDropdown` in SMF applets
- Do **not** use native `<select>` in modals (see `no-modal-native-select-controls.mdc`)

## Tab bar

**Canonical pattern:** table-based tab bar via `dsapSmfBuildTabBar()` (Security Center style).

**Default layout:** each tab is **equal width** across the bar (`table-layout: fixed` on `.dsap-smf-tabbar`; flex bars use `flex: 1 1 0`). Do not override per-applet unless there is a documented reason.

**Exception:** narrow or content-sized tabs (e.g. a `…` overflow tab) may use class `dsap-smf-tab-auto` on the cell/button, or `{ autoWidth: true }` on a tab entry in `dsapSmfBuildTabBar()`.

```javascript
dsapSmfBuildTabBar([
  { id: 'status', label: 'Status', icon: 'fas fa-gauge-high' },
  { id: 'phrasebook', label: 'Phrase Book', icon: 'fas fa-book' }
], activeTabId, { tabBarId: 'myTabBar', dataAttr: 'data-my-tab' });

dsapSmfWireTabBar(root, '#myTabBar', 'data-my-tab', (tabId) => buildUrl(tabId), host);
```

Flex tab bars (`.dsap-smf-tabbar-flex`, e.g. `omega-dsap-detail-tabbar`) share the same equal-width default; primary applet navigation should prefer the table tab bar.

## Root element

```html
<div data-dsap="my-applet" class="dsap-root dsap-smf my-applet">
```

## Markup helpers (`dsapSmfMarkup.js`)

- `dsapSmfBuildHeader({ branchTitle, toolTitle, logoSrc?, toolTitleId? })`
- `dsapSmfUpdateHeaderTool(dsapRoot, toolTitle, toolTitleId?)`
- `dsapSmfBuildTabBar(tabs, activeTabId, options?)`
- `dsapSmfBuildContextBar(html)` — workspace/scope strip (optional; avoid duplicating tab bar)
- `dsapSmfBuildToolbar(html, toolbarId?)`
- `dsapSmfBuildStatsTable(cells, tableId?)`
- `dsapSmfBuildSectionHdr(text, sectionId?)`
- `dsapSmfBuildStatusBox(messageHtml, boxId?, messageId?)`
- `dsapSmfWireTabBar(root, selector, dataAttr, urlBuilder, host)`

## CSS tokens (on `.dsap-smf`)

`--dsap-smf-bg`, `--dsap-smf-header-bg`, `--dsap-smf-header-tool-bg`, `--dsap-smf-tab-accent`, etc. — see `public/css/dsap-smf.css`.

## Class naming

| Component | Class |
|-----------|-------|
| Root | `.dsap-smf` + `.dsap-root` |
| Header | `.dsap-smf-header`, `.dsap-smf-header-branch`, `.dsap-smf-header-tool` |
| Tabs | `.dsap-smf-tabbar`, `.dsap-smf-tab`, `.dsap-smf-tab-active` |
| Toolbar | `.dsap-smf-toolbar` |
| Buttons | `.dsap-smf-btn`, `.dsap-smf-btn-primary`, `.dsap-smf-btn-danger` |

Legacy aliases (`sec-dsap-*`, `quips-dsap-*`, `memories-*`, `omega-dsap-*`) remain during migration; new markup should use `dsap-smf-*` names.

## Home landing

`dreamscape.jp` → `public/scripts/comp/dreamscapeHomeDsap.js` (registered at startup). This is the **Dreamscape tools hub** — SMF management tools only (no Grimoire Encyclopedia or Novels links on this page).

Grimoire home (`en.grimoire.jp`) has a **Settings** button next to Search the Grim that opens `dsap://dreamscape.jp/`.

## Reference applets

- **Tabs + layout:** Security Center (`securityCenterDsapApplet.js`)
- **Context menus:** Image Search filter pickers (`omegasearchDsapApplet.js`)
- **Header branch pattern:** Knowledge Memories (`memoriesDsapApplet.js`)
- **Tabbed tool:** Dynamic Quips (Status / Phrase Book / Configuration), Knowledge Memories (Memories / Rules / Configuration)

After CSS changes: `bash scripts/notify-service-worker-update.sh`
